\description{
Computes the Residual Cancer Burden (RCB) index and class (Symmans et al.,
2007) from the standard post-neoadjuvant pathology variables: the two
dimensions of the primary tumour bed, overall cancer cellularity, the
in-situ fraction, the number of positive lymph nodes, and the diameter of
the largest nodal metastasis. The continuous index is classified into RCB-0
(pathologic complete response), RCB-I (minimal), RCB-II (moderate), and
RCB-III (extensive) residual disease using the established cut points (1.36
and 3.28). Works on a cohort (one row per patient) or as a single-case
calculator, and can optionally relate RCB class to a survival outcome.
}
